schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: How Web3 Relates to Your Existing Work
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    A short orientation piece framing web3 as an addition to an
    organization's existing mission-driven work (community relationships,
    program delivery, physical presence), not a replacement for it. Offers a
    pain-point-matching exercise across four areas (fundraising, transparency,
    coordination, community building) mapping each to a corresponding web3
    tool category (crypto donations, blockchain transparency, DAOs/governance
    tools, tokens/credentials), and recommends starting with one small,
    reversible use case (a crypto-donate button, a Snapshot vote, a POAP, an
    on-chain published budget) rather than rebuilding everything.
  audience: mission-driven organizations and community groups new to web3
  known_tensions: []
  related_concepts:
    - web3-as-addition-not-replacement
  related_resources: []
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/relates-to-existing-work.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
